# Terraform
.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
# Terraform plan files. A plan embeds a full state snapshot, so committing one
# publishes every credential Terraform holds. Named without an extension by
# convention, which is also why no content scanner looks inside them: gitleaks
# decides what is an archive from the extension, so a plan file scans as zero
# bytes and reports nothing.
tfplan
*.tfplan
*.plan.out
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
# terraform.tfvars is generated by create-koras-app and holds no secrets —
# profile, slug, enabled components, regions. Secrets reach Terraform through
# TF_VAR_* from a Doppler-injected shell and are never written to a file.
!infrastructure/terraform/terraform.tfvars
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Environment / secrets — NEVER commit these. Doppler is the sole authority.
.env
.env.*
!.env.*.example
!.env.local.example
doppler.yaml

